# Build context is the repo root so the Dockerfile can COPY src/ plus the lockfile.
# Everything else would only thrash the layer cache on a docs edit.
*
!src/
!SKILL.md
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
# mcp/ is here for mcp/Dockerfile, which installs the wrapper from this checkout rather
# than from PyPI (#475) and shares the repo root as its context. docker/Dockerfile does
# not COPY it, so the only cost to the service image is a context hash that also moves
# when the wrapper changes.
!mcp/
# ...but not what building the Worker leaves inside it. `pywrangler dev|deploy` writes a
# CPython venv, a Pyodide venv, the vendored wheel set it bundles (884 files, ~20 MB of
# emscripten wheels including wasm32 `.so` binaries) and miniflare's local state; the
# `$schema` in wrangler.jsonc also invites a `node_modules/`. Together that is well over
# 100 MB. `!mcp/` is a directory re-include, so without these the whole lot joins the
# build context for BOTH Dockerfiles at the repo root — and `mcp/Dockerfile`'s `COPY mcp/`
# would bake it into a layer that the later `rm -rf` cannot shrink. Gitignored too, but
# these are separate lists and only this one governs what Docker uploads.
mcp/worker/.venv
mcp/worker/.venv-workers
mcp/worker/python_modules
mcp/worker/.wrangler
mcp/worker/node_modules
mcp/worker/pylock.toml
mcp/worker/bundle.log
mcp/dist
mcp/worker/.dev.vars
